  array (
    'id_section' => 204,
    'id_page' => 2,
    'type_section' => 'timeline',
    'titre_section' => 'Our Vision 2026-2031 (Milestones) ',
    'sous_titre' => 'Our Vision 2026-2031 (Milestones) ',
    'contenu_texte' => '<ul>
<li><span style="font-size: 14pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><strong>1) Research &amp; Product Development</strong></span><br><strong>2026:</strong> Complete bioactive compound identification for top 5 chronic disease targets (oncology, diabetes, cardiovascular).<br><strong>2027:</strong> Preclinical validation (mechanism-of-action, safety, efficacy) of lead compounds.<br><strong>2028:</strong> Submission of first regulatory dossiers for clinical trials.</li>
<li><strong><span style="font-size: 14pt;">2) Clinical &amp; Healthcare Services</span></strong><br><strong>2026&ndash;2027: </strong>Launch pilot on-site herbal clinic in capital city + online health consultation platform (phone, form-based, video) for domestic and regional coverage.<br><strong>2027&ndash;2028: </strong>Expand to 5 additional domestic clinics.<br><strong>2028&ndash;2030:</strong> Establish "AGF ONE" AI-assisted platform (Application) to provide a global AI-powered platform for learning, health, marketplace, and community engagement, while enabling scalable revenue tracking and growth.<br><strong>2029:</strong> Begin first clinical trial in collaboration with regional or international hospital networks.</li>
<li><span style="font-size: 14pt;"><strong>3) Community Training &amp; Capacity Building</strong></span><br><strong>2026:</strong> Develop community training curriculum for commercial organic farming of medicinal plants.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <strong>2027:</strong> Train first 500 community members in medicinal plant cultivation and post-harvest processing.<br><strong>2028&ndash;2030: </strong>Scale to train 5,000 community members across Zambia and COMESA region.</li>
<li><span style="font-size: 14pt;"><strong>4) Preventive Nutrition &amp; Health Education</strong></span><br>2026: Launch multi-channel awareness campaigns (TV, radio, social media) on preventive nutrition and home remedies.<br>2027&ndash;2028: Reach 50,000 community members via campaigns and workshops.<br>2029&ndash;2031: Scale awareness programs across Southern Africa with digital platforms (WhatsApp, YouTube, Facebook, TikTok).</li>
<li><span style="font-size: 14pt;"><strong>5) Manufacturing &amp; Quality Assurance</strong></span><br><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;"><em><strong>2026:</strong> Construct and equip GMP-aligned phytopharmaceutical production facility.</em></span><br><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;"><em><strong>2027:</strong> Obtain GMP and GLP certifications.</em></span><br><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;"><em><strong>2028:</strong> Begin commercial production of standardized herbal medicines.</em></span><br><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;"><em><strong>2029&ndash;2031: </strong>Achieve batch-to-batch consistency, full traceability, and supply to domestic and international markets.</em></span></li>
<li><span style="font-size: 14pt;"><strong>6) Partnerships &amp; Funding</strong></span><br><em><strong>2026&ndash;2027:</strong> Sign domestic and regional partnerships for research, training, and clinical networks.</em><br><em><strong>2027&ndash;2028: </strong>Establish key international scientific and technical partnerships (universities, GLP labs, clinical networks).</em><br><em><strong>2028&ndash;2031:</strong> Secure blended finance and institutional impact funding (DFIs, IFC, Gates Foundation).</em></li>
<li><span style="font-size: 14pt;"><strong>7) Impact &amp; Scaling</strong></span><br><strong>2028:</strong> Reach first 50,000 patients/clients with herbal and digital health services.<br><strong>2029&ndash;2031:</strong> Expand ecosystem to cover multiple chronic diseases across Zambia, Southern Africa, and select international markets.<br><strong>2031:</strong> AGF fully recognized as a regional leader in standardized phytopharmaceuticals and community health empowerment, with measurable social and health impact metrics.</li>
<li>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: left; line-height: 107%; margin: 0cm 0cm .15pt -.25pt;" align="left"><span style="font-size: 18pt;"><strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;">8)</strong><strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;"><span style="font-family: \'Arial\',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial;"> </span>Summary: </strong></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: left; text-indent: 0cm; line-height: 107%; margin: 0cm 0cm .4pt 18.0pt;" align="left"><strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;"><span style="mso-spacerun: yes;">&nbsp;</span></strong></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0cm 0cm .85pt -.25pt;"><strong>These milestones translate AGF&rsquo;s objectives into concrete, measurable checkpoints, covering research, clinical services, community training, manufacturing, partnerships, and impact, making progress visible to investors, donors, and regulators.</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>',
